    "created_at": "2025-02-28T21:29:43Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-02-28T21:29:43Z",
    "body": "The solution I use is to load Starship only if we are not in a \"dumb\" terminal session.\n\nFor `bash` or `zsh`:\n\n```shell\nif [[ \"$TERM\" != \"dumb\" ]]; then\n  eval \"$(starship init zsh)\"\nfi\n```\n\nFor `fish`:\n\n```fish\nif test $TERM != \"dumb\"\n  starship init fish | source\nend\n```",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
